# Keyboard and nav-button backlight logic, ported from LOS23.
#
# Supersedes the earlier kbd-backlight-inverse-lcd.patch, which covered
# only the brightness curve. Both patches touched the same region of
# updateDisplayPowerStateLocked, so keeping them separate made the apply
# order load-bearing for no benefit. This one file now carries the whole
# feature.
#
# Source: tim-ecoder/android_frameworks_base, branch lineage-23.2-athena,
# commits 8a9d56b294c0, a24fad886c47, 7c9f72746ab3, 6f9153d21778.
#
# WHAT IT DOES
#
# 1. Inverse-LCD curve for the KEYBOARD backlight only:
#      screen <= 0     -> kbd off
#      screen <= 3     -> kbd at 120/255 (darkroom, don't blind the user)
#      screen <  50    -> kbd full
#      screen >= 50    -> kbd off (daylight, invisible anyway)
#    Nav-buttons deliberately keep their unscaled slider value so they stay
#    visible in daylight.
#
# 2. BUTTON_BACKLIGHT_TIMEOUT now also governs the keyboard LED. Previously
#    the mKeyboardLight branch was a one-shot setBrightness with no timeout,
#    so the keyboard LED never switched itself off after typing stopped.
#
# 3. The keyboard timer is driven by its own timestamp (mLastKbdActivityTime
#    in PowerGroup), recorded only for EVENT_BUTTON / EVENT_OTHER coming from
#    SYSTEM_UID. EVENT_OTHER covers the physical QWERTY keys and the keyboard
#    touchpad, EVENT_BUTTON the capacitive nav-button row. Sharing
#    mLastButtonActivityTime instead would let any screen tap relight the
#    keyboard; dropping the uid filter would let app-driven userActivity
#    (MediaSession, Choreographer) keep it lit forever.
#
# 4. mKeyboardVisible no longer gates the keyboard LED. It is driven by the
#    LID switch, which is meaningless on athena - the keyboard is always
#    physically present, so the gate only ever turned the light off.
#
# mButtonTimeout == 0 means no timeout: the LEDs stay lit while the screen
# is on. That is what the "Enabled (no timeout)" entry of the BlackBerry
# keyboard DeviceSettings menu selects, and it is the default there.

